# 12 — Moonshots / Beyond-Release Backlog

These are not reasons to delay core reliability, but architecture should not make them impossible.

## Living world history
- [ ] multi-year/century coarse simulation of forests, settlements, roads, rivers, architecture, economy;
- [ ] historical age cohorts after floods/fire/clearing;
- [ ] building aging, renovation and settlement expansion;
- [ ] tree developmental history, scars, storm/pruning memory, lineage;
- [ ] regional trade and demographic/family generations;
- [ ] climate/ecological migration and river-channel change;
- [ ] world-history timeline and optional inspection of earlier states.

## Deep botany/ecology
- [ ] deterministic genotype/phenotype: genetics × environment × age × management;
- [ ] heritable bounded offspring/cultivars/mutation;
- [ ] hydraulic/resource allocation and source/sink approximation;
- [ ] bud bank, epicormic shoots, reaction wood, coppice/pollard/grafting;
- [ ] mycorrhizal/network abstractions, nurse logs/rocks, microhabitats;
- [ ] seed dispersal by wind/water/animal/gravity and clonal colonies;
- [ ] decomposition stages and habitat cavities/perches/nests.

## Deep environment
- [ ] long-term erosion/geomorphology and climate-dependent terrain evolution;
- [ ] detailed snow drift/ice accumulation/snow shedding;
- [ ] wildfire-weather/fuel ecology where appropriate;
- [ ] flood/landslide/avalanche/rockfall history shaping vegetation/roads;
- [ ] coast/tide/salinity systems and waterspouts where applicable.
